<https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "Gibson, J.J. (1979). The Ecological Approach to Visual Perception, ch. 8." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A relational property between an actor and the system: what the coupled actor+system can accomplish through the system's real surfaces. Gibsonian; actor-relative; eval-verified." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Affordance" .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Signifier> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> "Norman, D. (2013). The Design of Everyday Things, revised ed., preface." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Signifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Signifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Signifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A perceivable cue on a specific surface that indicates to an actor that an action is available here: GUI button, palette entry, keybinding label, CLI --help text, hint, icon. The perceivable aspect of an affordance." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Signifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Signifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Signifier" .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Surface> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Surface> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Surface> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A protocol or interface through which actors and readers meet the system. Two directions share the word. INBOUND surfaces are the invocation faces through which an actor reaches the system to act — MCP, CLI, SDK, GUI, keyboard, voice, palette (the descriptor detail is operation-surface's). OUTBOUND surfaces are the faces onto which a Publication projects a region of the graph for readers (publishedOn -> Surface): x0k-native (the document/motif renderer) or an external protocol (DFOS, ActivityPub, ATProto, IndieWeb). An external outbound surface additionally carries a direction (one-way syndication, or two-way where inbound replies fold back into the graph as observations) and an identity face (the owner's did:key projected as that network's own identity). See decisions/architecture/surfaces/publication-projection.md." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Surface> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#Surface> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Surface" .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#claimedFor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#claimedFor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#claimedFor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Actor kind(s) for which the affordance's claim is made. (Affordance, Actor) is a distinct verifiable tuple — the same underlying techne may afford different things to different actors, and those are separate claims." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#claimedFor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#claimedFor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#defines> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#defines> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#defines> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Design defines the affordances that follow from its experience-shape decision. The affordance is then verified independently by its literate spec; the design is realized when a publication ships the modules that enable them." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#defines> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Design> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#defines> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#defines> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> .
