<https://0k.computer/ontology#presentsSignifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Signifier> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#proves> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#proves> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#proves> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The chunk that tangles a test proves an affordance: authored as the proves= attribute on the code block declaring the test, addressed as <implementation id>#<chunk name>, so the proof lives on the code and a renamed or deleted test is a dangling edge the checker reports. The affordance's verifiedBy is the derived dual; nothing on a design names a test. Status is derived from it: proven when a proving chunk's tests ran green at projection, declared when the affordance has a face and no proof, claimed when it has neither." .
