<https://0k.computer/ontology#proves> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#proves> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#publishedOn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#publishedOn> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#publishedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Surface on which this Publication is published: wherever the region meets its audience — a runtime listener bound to one configuration, a repository host, a package registry, a release channel, an operating system its modules are built to run on." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#publishedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Publication> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#publishedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#publishedOn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Surface> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#requires> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#requires> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#requires> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Affordance requires Affordance: the second affordance must already hold for the first to hold. Affordance dependency graph; distinct from Techne dependsOn (substrate composition) and Decision dependsOn (decision rests on decision). Many-to-many; transitive at query time." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#requires> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#requires> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#requires> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#signifies> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#signifies> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#signifies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A signifier signifies an affordance — it is the perceivable cue (button, label, keybinding hint, default suggestion) that indicates to an actor that the affordance is available here. Techne realizes the affordance; signifier signifies it. The two together make the affordance both real and reachable; either alone is incomplete (techne without signifier is unreachable for perception-dependent actors; signifier without techne is a broken promise)." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#signifies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Signifier> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#signifies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#signifies> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Affordance> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#verifiedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#verifiedBy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://0k.computer/ontology#Concept> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#verifiedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "What proves an affordance holds: an executable spec at any rung - a LiterateSpec the eval harness drives, or a chunk of an Implementation that tangles a test and declares proves= for it (the derived dual of proves). The admissible targets are a shape on software; the term itself has no range, because the two classes live in document and the constraint is contextual (vocabulary-shapes §3)." .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#verifiedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> _:b0000n0000 .
<https://0k.computer/ontology#verifiedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://0k.computer/ontology/software> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology/software> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://0k.computer/ontology/software> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The publishable slice of the infrastructure domain: Affordance, Signifier, Surface, and the edges among them and the document genus. Split out of product (ontology-modules §2) so a publication that ships core and document can ship the affordance vocabulary its documents use without importing work or actor. Keeps the base namespace, like product. SoftwareModule stays in product: it is rdfs:subClassOf Artifact, which work defines." .
